AWS-015 — Workflow Optimization

Document ID: AWS-015
Title: Workflow Optimization
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Workflow Optimization Model (CWOM-O) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Workflow Optimization Model establishes the principles, architecture, analysis methods, governance mechanisms, and continuous improvement processes required to optimize Workflow Definitions, Workflow Instances, Workflow Programs, and execution environments while preserving engineering intent, governance, explainability, and execution reproducibility.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Workflow optimization architecture
Performance analysis
Bottleneck detection
Process mining
Simulation
Optimization recommendations
AI-assisted optimization
Continuous improvement

This specification applies to every governed Workflow Definition and Workflow Program.

3. Canonical Definition

Workflow Optimization is the governed analysis and improvement of workflow definitions, execution strategies, and orchestration based on objective operational evidence while preserving engineering intent, governance, and execution integrity.

Workflow Optimization improves future execution.

It SHALL NOT modify historical Workflow Instances.

4. Objectives

The Workflow Optimization Model SHALL:

Improve workflow performance.
Reduce operational inefficiency.
Eliminate bottlenecks.
Increase execution reliability.
Support AI-assisted recommendations.
Preserve governance.
Maintain explainability.
Enable continuous improvement.
5. Optimization Principles

Every workflow optimization SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Evidence-Based

Optimization SHALL be based upon measurable operational evidence.

Explainability

Every optimization recommendation SHALL explain:

Why improvement is recommended.
Expected benefits.
Supporting evidence.
Potential risks.
Non-Destructive

Optimization SHALL NOT alter historical execution records.

Governance

Optimization SHALL comply with applicable Canonical Policy Objects.

Repeatability

Equivalent optimization inputs SHALL produce equivalent recommendations.

Human Oversight

Recommendations affecting workflow semantics SHOULD require human review unless an autonomous optimization profile explicitly authorizes automated adoption.

