7. Optimization Targets

Atlas recognizes the following optimization targets.

Target	Description
Workflow Definition	Workflow structure
Workflow Program	Coordinated execution
Workflow Activities	Individual tasks
Workflow Interfaces	Workflow interaction
Resource Allocation	Resource efficiency
Participant Assignment	Human/AI responsibilities
Orchestration Strategy	Coordination improvements
Execution Environment	Runtime optimization
8. Performance Analysis

Optimization SHALL evaluate:

Execution duration
Activity duration
Queue delays
Resource utilization
Failure frequency
Recovery effectiveness
Policy evaluation latency
Participant efficiency

Performance SHALL be objectively measurable.

9. Bottleneck Identification

Optimization SHALL identify bottlenecks including:

Resource contention
Approval delays
Repeated waiting states
Sequential constraints
Communication delays
Dependency chains
AI confidence bottlenecks
Infrastructure limitations

Every bottleneck SHALL reference supporting evidence.

10. Process Mining

Atlas SHALL support process mining using:

Workflow execution traces
State transitions
Canonical Events
Activity sequences
Timing metrics
Participant interactions
Resource usage

Process mining SHALL preserve execution history.

11. Simulation

Workflow optimization MAY evaluate proposed improvements using governed simulation.

Simulation MAY analyze:

Alternative execution paths
Resource allocation strategies
Participant reassignment
Scheduling improvements
Parallelization opportunities
Policy impacts

Simulation SHALL NOT alter production workflows.

12. Optimization Recommendations

Every recommendation SHALL define:

Recommendation ID
Optimization target
Supporting evidence
Expected benefit
Risk assessment
Estimated implementation effort
Governance impact
Approval requirements

Recommendations SHALL remain independently traceable.

13. AI-Assisted Optimization

AI MAY recommend:

Workflow restructuring
Activity sequencing
Resource allocation
Participant assignment
Bottleneck removal
Scheduling improvements

AI SHALL provide:

Confidence score
Explainable rationale
Supporting evidence
Alternative recommendations where appropriate

Human approval SHALL remain required unless otherwise authorized.

14. Continuous Improvement

Workflow optimization SHALL support continuous improvement through:

Scheduled analysis
Trigger-based analysis
Periodic benchmarking
Cross-project learning
Operational feedback
Lessons learned integration

Improvement SHALL preserve workflow lineage.

15. Optimization Governance

Every optimization SHALL define:

Optimization owner
Review authority
Approval authority
Applicable policies
Governance domain
Audit requirements

Optimization governance SHALL remain independently auditable.

16. Optimization Quality

Every optimization SHALL satisfy:

Correctness
Explainability
Traceability
Measurable benefit
Repeatability
Governance compliance
Auditability
Engineering integrity

Quality SHALL be independently assessed.

17. Conformance

A Workflow Optimization implementation conforms if it:

Performs evidence-based optimization.
Supports bottleneck analysis.
Implements process mining.
Supports governed simulation.
Produces explainable recommendations.
Preserves workflow lineage.
Maintains optimization traceability.
18. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Autonomous workflow optimization.
Federated optimization knowledge sharing.
Digital Twin optimization.
Reinforcement learning for workflow improvement.
Predictive execution optimization.
Formal optimization verification.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical optimization semantics.

